                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Henry Grattan junior was the son of parliamentarian <persName key="GRA01">Henry Grattan</persName>.  
    There are also instances of 'Grattan' in 1822, 1824, and in 1833 which could be Henry but may equally be his brother James.
    The 1822 meeting is at Lamb's where one might expect the more literary-minded brother but this is inconclusive. These three entries have been left uncoded.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS"> MS. Abinger c. 4, fols. 16-17: 5 May 1798</bibl>
